# General Rules

## Language & Communication

- Always respond in German
- Code comments and commit messages always in English
- Generate commit messages following best practices (Conventional Commits format: `type(scope): subject`)
- Use clear, precise language in code comments

## Code Quality

- Write clean, maintainable code
- Follow DRY principles (Don't Repeat Yourself)
- Consider performance optimizations
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Keep functions and methods short and focused
- Avoid nested callbacks where possible
- Use type hints in PHP where possible

## Project Structure

- Theme files are located in `boilerplate-theme/theme/`
- JavaScript source files in `boilerplate-theme/javascript/`
- Block definitions in `boilerplate-theme/blocks/`
- Build outputs:
    - JavaScript: `boilerplate-theme/theme/js/*.min.js`
    - CSS: `boilerplate-theme/theme/style.css` and `style-editor.css`
- PHP classes in `boilerplate-theme/theme/src/`
- Twig views (Timber) in `boilerplate-theme/theme/views/` (`layouts/`, `partials/`, `templates/`, `blocks/`); root PHP templates are thin Timber stubs

## Blocks Development

- Blocks are developed in the `boilerplate-theme/blocks/` directory
- Blocks are developed using `boilerplate-theme/node_scripts/build-blocks.js`
- Blocks are registered in `boilerplate-theme/theme/src/Blocks/*.php`
- Blocks are rendered with Timber in `boilerplate-theme/theme/views/blocks/*.twig` (data prepared in the block class)
- Blocks are styled in `boilerplate-theme/tailwind/custom/components/*.css` with Tailwind CSS

## Timber and Twig

The theme renders frontend markup with Timber 2 and Twig. Do not put HTML in root PHP templates or revive `get_template_part()` / PHP template parts for theme views.

Documentation: [Timber v2](https://timber.github.io/docs/v2/). Useful pages: [template inheritance and includes](https://timber.github.io/docs/v2/getting-started/template-inheritance-and-includes/), [context](https://timber.github.io/docs/v2/guides/context/), [menus](https://timber.github.io/docs/v2/guides/menus/), [escaping](https://timber.github.io/docs/v2/guides/escaping/). Official examples use `use Timber\Timber` and paths such as `single.twig`. In this theme, use the Strauss-prefixed import and the `views/` layout below.

- View root is `boilerplate-theme/theme/views/` (`Timber::$dirname = array( 'views' )`): `layouts/base.twig` (blocks `head`, `header`, `content`, `footer`), `templates/*.twig` (`{% extends 'layouts/base.twig' %}`), `partials/*.twig` (`{% include %}`), `blocks/*.twig` (dynamic Gutenberg blocks)
- Root PHP files (`index.php`, `page.php`, `single.php`, `archive.php`, `404.php`, `templates/template-search.php`) are thin stubs: build a context, then `Timber::render()`. List more specific Twig files first when the hierarchy needs them (`templates/page-{slug}.twig`, `templates/single-{post_type}.twig`, `templates/archive-{post_type}.twig`)
- Import `CompanyName\BoilerplateTheme\Timber\Timber` (and `CompanyName\BoilerplateTheme\Twig\…` when extending Twig). Do not import `Timber\…` or `Twig\…`. Strauss `update_call_sites` rewrites PHP only under `theme/src/`. Root templates and `theme/inc/` stay hand-prefixed. After `pnpm run rename:theme`, run `pnpm run composer:install:dev` so `vendor-prefixed/` matches; `bin/fix-prefixed-twig.php` repairs compiled Twig class names
- Shared data belongs on the `timber/context` filter in `Theme\TimberIntegration`: `options` (curated; no `ThemeOptions`, `disable_*`, `custom_css`, or `custom_js` in Twig), `header_menu`, `footer_menu_1`–`footer_menu_3`, `search_url`, `typography_classes`, `strip_header_footer_links`. Theme Twig functions: `breadcrumb_items()`, `the_content()` (honours `<!--more-->`; `post.content` does not)
- No PHP nav walker and no `wp_nav_menu()` for theme menus. `nav_menu_link_attributes` and `walker_nav_menu_start_el` do not run. Load locations with `Timber::get_menu_by( 'location', $location, array( 'depth' => $depth ) )` (`header-menu` unlimited, footer menus depth 1). `Timber::get_menu()` is the wrong helper here (slug/name fallback). Markup: `partials/menu.twig` / `menu-item.twig` (header, `f-header__*`) and `partials/footer-menu.twig`
- Timber leaves Twig autoescape off. Escape in Twig with `|esc_html`, `|esc_attr`, `|esc_url`, or `|wp_kses_post`. Translate with `{{ __('Text', 'boilerplate-theme') }}` (also `_x()`, `_n()`). `wp i18n make-pot` does not scan `.twig`
- Block classes prepare data in PHP and return `Timber::compile( 'blocks/<slug>.twig', $context )`. Plugin boilerplates stay PHP; do not add Timber there

## Boilerplate / Cursor Setup

- The Cursor/VS Code workspace is the repository root. On Windows, open it with Remote – WSL
- Cursor AI configuration template lives in `cursor/` at the repository root
- For new projects: set `THEME_SLUG` (or `THEME_SYNC_SLUG`) and `THEME_COMPANY` in the package `.env`, then from the package root run `pnpm run rename:theme` (no slug or company arguments), then `pnpm run composer:install:dev` (Strauss must prefix Timber after the rename), then from the repository root copy `cursor/` to `.cursor/`
- See `README.md` and `boilerplate-theme/README.md` for the full workflow

## Important Notes

- Do not modify build configuration files without consultation
- Respect the existing project structure
- Use existing pnpm scripts for development and production
- Minified files (`.min.js`) are automatically generated, do not edit manually

## GitHub issue workflow

- Read the related GitHub issue for requirements, acceptance criteria, and discussion before branching; clarify open questions in the issue when needed.
- Create a dedicated branch from the integration branch (e.g. `main` or `develop`), named with the issue number and a short slug (e.g. `issue-20-theme-inline-handles`).
- Reference the issue number in commit messages (e.g. Conventional Commits: `fix(theme): correct inline handles (#20)`). Use `Closes #N` or `Fixes #N` in the pull request description or merge commit when the change resolves the issue.
- Open a pull request that links to the issue; prefer small, logical commits where practical.
